{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"reasoning","text":"**Updating function with docstring and instrumentation**\n\n{\"code\": \"def compute_ttl_with_jitter(\\n    base_ttl: float = 300.0,\\n    jitter_range: float = 30.0,\\n) -> float:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Compute an effective TTL by applying random jitter.\\n\\n    The jitter is added to the base TTL to spread cache expiry across a\\n    window, preventing a coordinated stampede of cache misses. The\\n    operational metrics pipeline is notified via the `cache.ttl.jittered`\\n    metric whenever a jittered TTL is computed.\\n\\n    Parameters\\n    ----------\\n    base_ttl:\\n        The base time-to-live in seconds.\\n    jitter_range:\\n        Maximum additional jitter in seconds. The actual jitter is\\n        drawn uniformly from [0, jitter_range).\\n\\n    Returns\\n    -------\\n    float\\n        The effective TTL in seconds.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    jitter = random.uniform(0, jitter_range)\\n    effective_ttl = base_ttl + jitter\\n    from . import metrics\\n    metrics.increment(\\\"cache.ttl.jittered\\\")\\n    return effective_ttl\\n\", \"comments\": \"Jitter now adds to base TTL and the cache.ttl.jittered metric is emitted.\"}"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"code\": \"def compute_ttl_with_jitter(\\n    base_ttl: float = 300.0,\\n    jitter_range: float = 30.0,\\n) -> float:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Compute an effective TTL by applying random jitter.\\n\\n    The jitter is added to the base TTL to spread cache expiry across a\\n    window, preventing a coordinated stampede of cache misses. The\\n    operational metrics pipeline is notified via the `cache.ttl.jittered`\\n    metric whenever a jittered TTL is computed.\\n\\n    Parameters\\n    ----------\\n    base_ttl:\\n        The base time-to-live in seconds.\\n    jitter_range:\\n        Maximum additional jitter in seconds.  The actual jitter is\\n        drawn uniformly from [0, jitter_range).\\n\\n    Returns\\n    -------\\n    float\\n        The effective TTL in seconds.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    jitter = random.uniform(0, jitter_range)\\n    effective_ttl = base_ttl + jitter\\n    from . import metrics\\n    metrics.increment(\\\"cache.ttl.jittered\\\")\\n    return effective_ttl\\n\", \"comments\": \"Add the jitter to the base TTL and emit the cache.ttl.jittered metric for each computation.\"}"}}
